---
import "../styles/global.css";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/base-layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/site-header.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/site-footer.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={`Privacy policy for ${siteConfig.name}.`}
  canonicalUrl={`https://${siteConfig.domain}/privacy`}
  siteName={siteConfig.name}
  themeColor={siteConfig.theme.primary}
>
  <SiteHeader
    slot="header"
    siteName={siteConfig.name}
    navItems={siteConfig.nav?.items}
    ctaText={siteConfig.funnel.bofu.ctaText}
    ctaHref={siteConfig.funnel.bofu.ctaTarget}
  />

  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-brand-text)] mb-2">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-brand-muted)] mb-8">
      Effective date: June 3, 2026
    </p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-[var(--color-brand-muted)]">
      <h2>Who We Are and Our Role</h2>
      <p>
        Gavelhouse is HOA and condo software operated by {
          siteConfig.legalEntity
        } ("Gavelhouse", "we", "us"). We provide software to volunteer boards and
        self-managed community associations in the United States.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our role depends on whose data is involved. For data your community
        association enters into Gavelhouse about its homeowners and residents,
        the association is the data controller (and, under California law, the
        "business"), and we act as its service provider / processor &mdash; we
        process that data only to provide the service on the association's
        instructions, and we do not sell or share it. For data we collect
        directly about board members and account holders who sign up, for our
        billing relationship, and for marketing leads, we act as the controller.
      </p>

      <h2>Whose Data We Process</h2>
      <p>
        Gavelhouse processes personal data about: (a) board members, treasurers,
        administrators, and other users who hold an account; (b) homeowners and
        residents whose records a board enters or imports into the platform,
        including through the owner portal; and (c) prospective customers who
        contact us or download a resource.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Account and authentication data.</strong> When you create a Gavelhouse
        account we collect your name, email address, and password (or, if you sign
        in with Google, your Google account identifier and profile image). For security
        and abuse prevention we also store session records that include IP address
        and browser user-agent.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Community data.</strong> We collect information about your community
        such as its name, units/addresses, and unit count, and we record board invitations
        and roles.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Homeowner and resident data (entered by the board).</strong> The platform
        stores homeowner first and last name, email address, phone number, move-in
        date, unit/property address, and ownership history. This data is provided
        by the community association, which is responsible for having a lawful basis
        to enter it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Financial and dues data.</strong> We store reserve and operating fund
        balances, budget and journal/ledger line items, bank reconciliation records,
        assessments, dues, and payment records (amount, method &mdash; ACH, card,
        check, or other &mdash; and date). Card and bank account numbers are handled
        by Stripe; Gavelhouse stores only payment metadata and Stripe identifiers,
        not full card or bank numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Governance and compliance records.</strong> We store violation and
        complaint records (including a title, description, status history, and any
        uploaded photos), architectural review requests (including descriptions and
        uploaded attachments), meetings, motions, and audit events. Uploaded photos
        and documents are stored as files in Cloudflare R2 object storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Support data.</strong> If you use the in-app AI support feature, we
        forward your account email and the content of your support messages to a Ventora
        customer-support service that uses an AI/LLM provider to generate a response.
        See "Sub-processors" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Marketing and usage data.</strong> If you submit a contact or lead-magnet
        form we store your email, the source page, any survey answers you provide,
        and a download record that may include IP address and user-agent. We also
        collect product and site analytics (pageviews, events, and device metadata)
        as described under "Cookies and Analytics".
      </p>

      <h2>How and Why We Use Data, and Legal Bases</h2>
      <p>
        We use personal data to: operate and secure the platform and your
        account (performance of a contract; our legitimate interest in
        security); process subscription billing and dues payments (performance
        of a contract; legal obligation for tax/accounting records); send
        transactional communications such as account, billing, and dues notices
        (performance of a contract); provide customer support, including the
        optional AI support feature (legitimate interest / your request); send
        marketing emails where you have opted in or as otherwise permitted, with
        an unsubscribe link in every message (consent or legitimate interest);
        and improve and debug the service (legitimate interest). Where we rely
        on consent, you may withdraw it at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell or share your personal data, and we do not use homeowner
        or community data for our own marketing. We may produce aggregated or
        de-identified statistics that cannot reasonably identify an individual
        or a community.
      </p>

      <h2>Sub-processors</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on the third-party sub-processors listed on our{" "}
        <a href="/subprocessors/" class="underline">Subprocessors page</a>,
        which include Cloudflare (hosting, Workers runtime, CDN, DNS, R2 object
        storage, and edge security), Neon (managed Postgres database), Stripe
        (subscription billing and dues payment processing), Resend
        (transactional and marketing email delivery), PostHog (product and site
        analytics), Sentry (error monitoring), Google (OAuth sign-in), Apollo
        (launch CRM for prospective-customer leads), and a Ventora-operated AI
        customer-support service backed by an AI/LLM provider. Each
        sub-processor handles data under its own terms and only as needed to
        provide its function to us.
      </p>

      <h2>International Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Gavelhouse is operated from the United States and stores data in the
        United States. If you access the service from outside the United States,
        your data will be transferred to and processed in the United States.
        Where required for transfers from the European Economic Area or United
        Kingdom, we and our sub-processors rely on appropriate safeguards such
        as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain account, community, governance, and financial records while
        your subscription is active and for as long as needed to provide the
        service. After an account is closed, we retain data only as long as
        needed and intend to delete or anonymize it within a reasonable period
        when it is no longer required, except where we are required to keep it
        longer (for example, financial and tax records) or where the community
        association instructs otherwise. Marketing leads are retained until you
        unsubscribe or request deletion.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Data is transmitted over encrypted TLS connections, and we run our
        application on Cloudflare's network with edge security controls.
        Authentication endpoints are rate-limited, and access to the production
        database is restricted. We store data with reputable infrastructure
        providers (Neon and Cloudflare) that maintain their own security
        programs. No system is perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee
        absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal
        data, and you may export your community's data from your account. To
        exercise these rights, contact us at the email below; we will verify
        your request and respond within the time required by applicable law.
        Because a community association controls homeowner records, requests
        about a specific homeowner may be directed to that association, and we
        will assist the association as its service provider.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>California (CCPA/CPRA).</strong> California residents may request
        the categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected,
        request deletion or correction, and are entitled not to be discriminated against
        for exercising these rights. We do not sell or share personal information
        as those terms are defined under the CCPA/CPRA.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>EEA/UK (GDPR).</strong> If you are in the European Economic Area or
        United Kingdom, you have rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction,
        portability, and objection, and the right to lodge a complaint with your supervisory
        authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Gavelhouse is a tool for community associations and is not directed to
        children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under
        13. If you believe a child's data has been provided to us, contact us
        and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use strictly necessary cookies to keep you signed in and to secure
        the service. We use PostHog for product and site analytics to understand
        how the platform is used. These analytics collect pageviews, events, and
        device metadata associated with a distinct identifier. We do not use
        third-party advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. When we make material
        changes, we will update the effective date above and, where appropriate,
        notify account holders.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy-related questions or data requests, contact our privacy
        contact, Angel Campa, at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.privacyEmail}`} class="underline">
          {siteConfig.privacyEmail}
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For enterprise customers requiring a Data Processing Agreement, see our{
          ""
        }
        <a href="/dpa/" class="underline">DPA page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the current list of subprocessors, see our{" "}
        <a href="/subprocessors/" class="underline">Subprocessors page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <SiteFooter
    slot="footer"
    siteName={siteConfig.name}
    tagline={siteConfig.tagline}
    linkGroups={siteConfig.footer?.linkGroups}
    legalLinks={siteConfig.footer?.legalLinks}
  />
</BaseLayout>
